(
 '# Start using APLGUI'
 ''
 'This page explains how best to start using `APLGUI`; we start from a CLEAR WS.'
 ''
 '~~~'
 ')LoadPackages [tatin]APLGUI'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'This loads `APLGUI` and all dependencies into the workspace under the name `APLGUI`.'
 'This is perfect for trying it out.'
 ''
 'In order to permanently work with `APLGUI` you must install it. For example, assuming'
 'that you have an application `Foo` that required `APLGUI` you would first install it,'
 'typically in a sub-folder of your project called `packages/`:'
 ''
 '~~~'
 ']InstallPackages [tatin]APLGUI'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'When you initialize your application you must execute:'
 ''
 '~~~'
 '⎕SE.Tatin.LoadDependencies /home/to/Foo/packages'
 '~~~'
 ''
 'And that''s it.'
)
